.TH WV 1 "July 2026" "weaverssh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wv \- bounded, bidirectional services over an authenticated SSH session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wv
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B wv
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B wv
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wv
is the unified command-line interface for weaverssh. It bootstraps through an
existing OpenSSH X11 channel, authenticates the X11 cookie, upgrades the stream
to WebSocket, and multiplexes bounded control, filesystem, TCP, UDP, event, and
policy services.
.PP
The dynamic-session path does not require operator-selected
.B ssh \-L
or
.B ssh \-R
ports. Signed node contexts identify the ordered topology and capabilities.
Local brokers are published as user-private IPC endpoints for other
.B wv
processes owned by the same account.
